{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63707-what-do-embeds-and-exploits-look-like","id":63707,"title":"What do Embeds and Exploits look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T20:00:11-08:00","id":63707,"title":"What do Embeds and Exploits look like?","content":"From reading the Kickstarter doc, I'm getting the impression that most Embeds and Exploits are fairly low-key. Trouble I'm having is this: I can visualize most of the WoD splat powers, vampires and mages and whatever. What does it look like when a Demon uses an Embed, Exploit or even a Gadget? What exactly happens? Is it more like coincidental magic or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T20:28:21-08:00","id":63719,"title":"","content":"Sometimes. Sometimes they're very clearly supernatural.<br /> <br /> If you're looking at exploits like Possession, flowing into a victim in the form of energy is pretty overt. Murder By Improbability, on the other hand, could be rather cartoony in execution but is also explained by rational, non-supernatural reasons. If anything, embeds seem to be a bit less obvious (with even the supernatural ones such as Hush still only local). Then again, look at an embed such as Tower of Babel. Demons' powers come from mucking around with the coding of the universe. Sometimes this is very specific and non-obvious. Other times, blood rains from the sky.<br /> <br /> Gadgets are mixed. An embedded gadget is as obviously supernatural as the embed used. Exploited gadgets are wacky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T21:24:29-08:00","id":63751,"title":"","content":"I imagine that embeds, in-general, are as you say, very low key and the specifics of certain embeds (i.e. the ones you or your players are likely to use) can be worked during play. <br /> Maybe I'd give some especially observant characters the slightest opportunity to detect that something happened. <br /> <br /> So maybe I'd let people with the unseen sense (not necessarily god-machine) or some other kind of very specific very special sense (probably not a mage sight or temporary power) to get this feeling of deja vu, like in the matrix. Or maybe cause an incredibly brief visual stutter like the world just replayed the last millisecond over. Or maybe the briefest taste of the air after lightning or a fleeting but strong smell from their childhood wafts past them. <br /> <br /> For exploits, they're always flashy in some way. From the super obvious rain of blood to the kind of stealthy murder by improbability. I agree with Jotun that murder by improbability may probably verge on the cartoon-y. Falling piano, space station detritus re-entering earth atmosphere, or perhaps something in the vein of final destination.<br /> <br /> Embeded gadgets &quot;remain outwardly unchanged from their original form&quot;.<br /> Installing an exploit into a gadget permanently changes the object making it very, very noticeable. You may be able to claim that it's a prop from a show or some kind of toy but it definitely stands out. (lifted from around 187 of the pdf).<br /> <br /> So say I installed an operating table with the exploit &quot;break to heal&quot;. The table may be warped to look super futuristic with an array of impressive looking surgical tools attached to robotic arms and a large receptacle may have been created under the table to accept material to be broken down and converted into energy/fuel/biomass to heal the target on the table. <br /> That's certainly very, very obvious. <br /> <br /> Bottom line, I think it's something you should discuss with your players and keep the following in mind. Embeds (and embedded gadgets) are super-low key, except for a couple of instances. Exploits (and exploited gadgets) are almost always really flashy in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T04:41:03-08:00","id":63875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/63707-what-do-embeds-and-exploits-look-like#post63707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From reading the Kickstarter doc, I'm getting the impression that most Embeds and Exploits are fairly low-key. Trouble I'm having is this: I can visualize most of the WoD splat powers, vampires and mages and whatever. What does it look like when a Demon uses an Embed, Exploit or even a Gadget? What exactly happens? Is it more like coincidental magic or what?</div> </div> </div> </div> Embeds are low key. They're supposed to be subtle magic (notable exception - On the Mend, which has gotten a number of complaints about being too flashy for an Embed). Stuff just seems to happen in their favor. Done right, there is nothing to notice or see. Demon wills it, coincidences happen.<br /> <br /> Gadgets are magical tools. They look like tools when used - think james bond super spy gadgets. They can either be obvious or flashy, depending if an embed or exploit is used.<br /> <br /> Exploits, however, are supposed to be blaring obvious uses of magic. Brute force. Its not chanting, but it is reality shaking. Peeks behind the Cover, perhaps, as glitches manifest. Demons don't appear to do magic like a mage chants, or a vampire making eye contact, or a werewolf snarling commands to spirits of his territory. They just suddenly manifest flame in their hands, or turn into shadows in a puff of brimstone. They unfurl wings and manifest horns, as if they'd just been hiding them behind coat or hair.<br /> <br /> Glitches, I feel, are the main source of &quot;look! Demon magic!&quot; stuff. I feel its kind of like a mage's nimbus peeking out when they cast a vulgar spell. They reach out, grab reality, remold it, and leave handprints behind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right now, the closest thing Demons have to ritual magic are their Exploits. That said, its theoretically possible to build Interface, even if the God Machine says &quot;No! Angels smash!&quot; I guess one could consider Interface a kind of ritual magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:08:01-08:00","id":63884,"title":"","content":"Ok. So the difference between an Embed and an Exploit is kind of like the difference between coincidental and vulgar magic? That makes the whole thing make a lot more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T12:36:21-08:00","id":69300,"title":"","content":"I visualized the &quot;Check Backdrop&quot; embed (p.133) as the last big shoot-out in Unforgiven.<br /> Lots of people shooting and missing a target right in front of them and one guy being deadly calm, aiming and killing one mook after the other. Shivers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1488-skeltem","name":"Skeltem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T12:31:48-08:00","id":69949,"title":"","content":"I find it useful to think of it this way - you'll note that most Embeds play with possibility.<br /> <br /> Everything that an Embed produces COULD have happened, in theory. Embeds play with quantum states. You'll never 'see' an Embed, unless you're a demon, in which case you might sense the Aether but you'd never see any sort of outward sign. A Demon that heals somebody with On The Mend doesn't touch them, doesn't treat them in any way... they're just present, and it turns out the injury 'wasn't that bad'. Every other Embed is the same - it's all stuff that -could- happen, just, the Demon chooses to make it a certainty rather than a variable.<br /> <br /> Essentially, what Demons do is kinda luck manipulation, but not quite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}